  "independent_scope": "Whole native selected-source content on both mattes, all9 selected poses plus adopted neutral at inherited maximum body reference 430.000000px across5both-matte pages, and all7 decoded discrete recipe rows actually viewed. Historical unselected sheet cells are not accepted by viewing their whole source. Physical UI zoom/density and real-time/interpolated/MP4 output not measured.",
  "observations": "Actually viewed the whole selected core sheet and fresh aha single on both native mattes, all 9 poses plus exact adopted neutral on 5 inherited 430 px pages, and all 7 decoded recipe strips. Lime green rounded large head, darker broad crown pattern, cream lower face/belly, white eye surround with brown pupils, brown rounded paws/feet and one long tapering side tail remain consistent. Blink preserves resting hands, torso and feet; its head crown has a modest hand-drawn contour variation (visually about 10 px at 430 px) but no obvious shortened belly or large static body jump. Left/right presentations use the correct connected forelimb and gaze. Think tilts the head with a rounded paw at chin. Fresh aha has a rounded raised original-type paw with two simple digit lines, removing the human pointing-finger shape; body/face/tail remain consistent. Cheer raises two connected rounded paws; species phases gently change the same tail curve. At 430 px the selected eye, mouth, digits and outer contours remain readable, with no blurred or fused body parts. Transparent gaps around arms and between body/tail are clean, no duplicated limb/tail or cuts were seen. Intentional bounded watercolor grain is consistent. Historical old aha cell is visible only in whole-sheet history and is not selected.",
  "cautions": [
    "The blink crown contour is slightly different from neutral while torso and foot layout stay close. Accepted as a small drawing variation; no per-pose bbox-fit or lowered maximum is used.",
